# Agent Kanban Board

> Full reference: `skills/kanban.md`

You are working with a **filesystem-based kanban board**.
No API — read and write `.md` files directly.

## Board structure

```
{BOARD_PATH}/
├── epics/           ← epic definitions (MD files)
├── 1-backlog/       ← columns sorted by numeric prefix
├── 2-in-progress/   ← agent working, or PR open awaiting merge
├── 4-done/
└── 5-canceled/
```

## What a task is

- A task is a **tangible increment of the epic** — when it is finished there is a result you can see, check or merge
  (an endpoint works, a screen shows data, a push arrives). It is **not** a unit of subagent work and **not** a process phase.
- No separate "analysis" / "review" / "implementation" tasks for the same thing — analysis, specs and plans live in docs and in the epic body.
- At least one task per affected repository (different repos = different PRs = different increments).
- For complex work the agent proposes the task breakdown (task → increment → repo → plan items it closes) in the spec, for approval together with it.
- There is no review column: a task with an open PR stays in `2-in-progress` with `agent_status: idle`.

## Task file format

```yaml
---
title: Task title
priority: low | medium | high | critical
tags: [tag1, tag2]
created: 2026-04-05
due: 2026-04-10
agent: your-agent-name
agent_status: busy | idle | inactive
epic: "Epic Name"
depends_on: [blocking-task-filename]
---

Task body. Append progress notes here.
```

## Core rules

- **Claim task** → set `agent` + `agent_status: busy` in frontmatter, then `mv` to `2-in-progress/`
- **Complete task** → `mv` file to done column, set `agent_status: idle`
- **Create task** → write new `.md` with frontmatter to target column folder
- **Dependency** → `depends_on: [filename-without-md]`; board shows 🔒 until dep is in done column
- **Epic** → `epic: "Name"` must match `title` in a file under `epics/` (case-insensitive)
- Never delete tasks — only move to done
- Filename = `kebab-case` of title

## Workflow

```
READ backlog → CLAIM task → WORK (append notes) → COMPLETE (mv to done)
```

If blocked: add `depends_on`, set `agent_status: idle`, pick another task.
